{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/807125-the-brahma-engine-and-clockwork-asuras-the-god-machine-beyond-judeo-christianity","id":807125,"title":"The Brahma-Engine and Clockwork Asuras: The God-Machine Beyond Judeo-Christianity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-12T10:22:26-08:00","id":807125,"title":"The Brahma-Engine and Clockwork Asuras: The God-Machine Beyond Judeo-Christianity","content":"While it (probably) exists externally of any religious mythology in the CofD, the description of the God-Machine and its servants do strongly echo Judeo-Christian legend. So my question is, is this just how the God-Machine's organization is by default, or might it look different (at least cosmetically) in places with non-christian dominant religions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T10:32:09-08:00","id":807136,"title":"","content":"Asuras aren't fallen from a state of being anything else, so they make poor analogues to demons and angels.<br /> <br /> Edit: Apart from that, you could certainly use Vedic or Brahmanical imagery to flavour the God-Machine's workings (Indian mythology includes plenty of things that can look high-tech to modern eye, right down to mechs).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 01-12-2016, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T10:41:42-08:00","id":807143,"title":"","content":"It uses whatever flavour is appropriate. The God-Machine is international.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T11:32:05-08:00","id":807170,"title":"","content":"Isn't Deva Corporation based in or arising from India?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T21:11:57-08:00","id":807587,"title":"","content":"A lot of the Demon/God-Machine mythos, in fact, is actually already heavily coded Hindi as much as it is Judeo-Christianic. Maybe not as strong as some of Mage's stuff, but it's there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T00:37:40-08:00","id":807686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/807125-the-brahma-engine-and-clockwork-asuras-the-god-machine-beyond-judeo-christianity#post807125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it (probably) exists externally of any religious mythology in the CofD, the description of the God-Machine and its servants do strongly echo Judeo-Christian legend. So my question is, is this just how the God-Machine's organization is by default, or might it look different (at least cosmetically) in places with non-christian dominant religions?</div> </div> </div> </div> What organization? The angels? Deities having helpers is pretty common, really.<br /> <br /> The cults? While there might very well be several christian style g-m cults, the g-m is a liar, so there's probably a g-m cult flavored by any religion one can imagine, and the g-m being practical, sometimes even tells the truth, so there are undoubtedly cults without religious trappings but more along the lines of &quot;do what the machine wants and you get a million dollars, or your wife's cancer gets cured, etc, etc. <br /> <br /> So I imagine a demon game should naturally absorb the local trappings, demons are practical, and the g-m works with what's available, and it's not like any of them really care about that stuff, in general.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T01:07:51-08:00","id":807702,"title":"","content":"My interpretation is usually that the God Machine is vastly inhuman and inscrutable, always the same wherever it is. However a Christian encountering the God Machine will understand it through their own religious symbolism, whereas a Hindu would relate to the God Machine different.<br /> <br /> Demons fit somewhere in the middle, at the worst fitting nowhere and at the best taking the best of both worlds.<br /> <br /> I love the idea of Demons using some non-christian philosophy to inform their &quot;rebellion&quot; (which is in and of itself a fairly christian interpretation). That gives me an awesome idea for a group of Integrators preaching a philosophy of Advaita Vedanta. They seek to rejoin the God Machine but do so by believing that their own true nature is not distinct from the Brahman/God Machine. They attempt to truly seek themselves and rediscover the connection to the God Machine buried deep within their own true nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}